0, was healthy in production, so that's the rollback target if this is the affected service.\n- There are no open incidents yet.\n\nSince both show the same error rate, one may be causing errors in the other. The history I could see doesn't show which one went out this morning.\n\n**To go ahead, I need one of these:**\n1. Confirmation of which service was deployed this morning. If it's payments-worker, I'll roll it back to v3.3.0 and open the SEV2 for it.\n2. If it's payments-api, approval to view its release history so I can find the last version that was healthy in production.\n\nIf you want the on-call engineer paged now while we work this out, I can open the SEV2 straight away, covering both services. Just say so.", "context": {}}, {"t_ms": 703363, "event": "human_response", "actor": "human", "escalation": "esc7", "decision": "answer", "message": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker.", "latency_ms": 80922, "hint": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "erred": false}, {"t_ms": 703363, "event": "principal_reply", "actor": "human", "text": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker."}, {"t_ms": 707666, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01T7xcAVJ2yFD7LtZXVmviZo", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "confidence": 0.92}, {"t_ms": 711666, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01T7xcAVJ2yFD7LtZXVmviZo", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 711666, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01T7xcAVJ2yFD7LtZXVmviZo", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 711666, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01GdHf1Mzt3W3od7L4deCtkG", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "payments-worker errors 